    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n49893" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Urbīnum</span></b> , i, n.,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a town in
				Umbria</i>, <i><span class="en">Tac. H. 3, 62</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Inscr.
					Orell. 3714</span></i>.—Hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Urbīnas</span></b> ,
				ātis, adj., <i>of</i> or <i>belonging to Urbinum</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Petissius,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Phil. 12, 8, 19</span></i>
			; cf. <i><span class="en">Varr. L. L. 8, § 84</span></i>
			Müll.—In plur.: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Urbī-nātes</span></b> ,
				um, m., <i>the
				inhabitants of Urbinum</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 3, 14,
				19, § 114</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Inscr. Orell.
				999</span></i>.</div>
